`pivot_rows(rows)` must transpose a rectangular list of row lists into a list of columns. Preserve row order within every column. An empty outer list or any number of empty rectangular rows returns `[]`. The returned cells must be deep copies, so nested mutable values do not alias the input or another independently copied cell. Do not mutate `rows`. Raise `ValueError` if the outer value is not a list, a row is not a list, or row lengths differ.

